---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Open source, for independent sitters"
  description="Boopity is an open-source project from Artwork Not Final LLC, made for independently run pet-care businesses."
>
  <article class="wrap max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-5 text-forest">About Boopity</p>
    <h1 class="display text-5xl sm:text-6xl">
      Your business.
      <br />
      Your own website.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-8 text-xl leading-relaxed">
      Boopity is open-source pet-sitting software from {site.owner}. It brings
      the basics of running a pet-care business into one installation you
      control.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">
      Not a marketplace. Not a subscription.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      There’s no central Boopity account or Boopity software subscription. You
      choose and pay for your own hosting, email delivery, and any payment
      processing. Each installation serves one business.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">Open to use and improve.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The application is MIT licensed. You can read the code, report a bug, or
      contribute an improvement. The license does not grant trademark rights.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link mt-5 inline-block" href={site.appRepository}>
      Explore the application on GitHub
    </a>
    <h2 id="support" class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold">
      A note on support
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Boopity is community-supported. Help and maintenance are best-effort, with
      no guaranteed response time. You or your installer are responsible for
      hosting, updates, backups, and testing your email and payment connections.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      For help, start with the{" "}
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/help/troubleshooting/">
        troubleshooting guide
      </a>
      . Follow the application’s{" "}
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://github.com/artwork-not-final/boopity/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
      >
        security policy
      </a>{" "}
      to report a vulnerability privately. Don’t put credentials or client
      information in a public issue.
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
